# Patch / install skills in Cursor (`~/.cursor/skills`)

When the user asks to **patch**, **upgrade**, **install**, or **refresh** skills (or you finish adding/changing skills in this repo), **run the Cursor install yourself** — do not only edit `skills/` in the clone.

**Source of truth:** `<repo>/skills/<name>/`  
**Cursor install target (default):** `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/`  
Use **per-project** `.cursor/skills/` only if the user explicitly wants project-local skills.

Do **not** copy skills into `<repo>/.cursor/skills/` — that duplicates the repo and breaks the install model.

## Skill bundle (install all together)

```
excalidraw-diagram
word-document
powerpoint-presentation
spreadsheet-document
pdf-document
_shared
```

- **New skill** in the repo → add its folder under `~/.cursor/skills/`.
- **Existing skill** (e.g. old Word/PPT) → **replace** the whole folder (`rm -rf` then `cp -a`) so stale `SKILL.md` / references are not left behind.
- **`_shared`** → always refresh when Word, PowerPoint, spreadsheet, or `office-tools` changed.

## Patch procedure (global Cursor)

Set `REPO` to this repository root, then:

```bash
REPO=/path/to/architect-doc-skill
CURSOR=~/.cursor/skills
BUNDLE="excalidraw-diagram word-document powerpoint-presentation spreadsheet-document pdf-document _shared"

mkdir -p "$CURSOR"

# Legacy Anthropic/tmp folder names — remove so Cursor does not load duplicates
for legacy in docx pptx xlsx pdf; do
  rm -rf "$CURSOR/$legacy"
done

# Replace every bundle folder (patch = full refresh)
for name in $BUNDLE; do
  rm -rf "$CURSOR/$name"
  cp -a "$REPO/skills/$name" "$CURSOR/$name"
done
```

## Verify

```bash
test -f "$CURSOR/_shared/office-tools/office_tools.py"
test -f "$CURSOR/word-document/SKILL.md"
test -f "$CURSOR/powerpoint-presentation/SKILL.md"
ls -1 "$CURSOR" | sort
find "$CURSOR" -maxdepth 2 -name .git -type d   # expect no output
```

Optionally `diff` installed `SKILL.md` against `$REPO/skills/*/SKILL.md`.

## After patching

1. Tell the user skills were updated under `~/.cursor/skills/`.
2. Ask them to **open a new agent chat** (or reload the window) so Cursor reloads `SKILL.md` descriptions.
3. Runtimes are separate: run `bash scripts/install_deps.sh` from the **repo clone**, not from `~/.cursor/skills/`.

Full paths, Copilot/Claude variants, and mistakes to avoid: [docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md](docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md).
